<article class="env-lemma" id="0AYX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AYX">Lemma <span data-tag="0AYX">33.44.7</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field, let $X$ be a proper scheme of dimension $\leq 1$ over $k$, and let $\mathcal{E}$, $\mathcal{V}$ be locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules of constant finite rank. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \deg (\mathcal{E} \otimes \mathcal{V}) = \text{rank}(\mathcal{E}) \deg (\mathcal{V}) + \text{rank}(\mathcal{V}) \deg (\mathcal{E})  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0AYW" data-tag="0AYW">33.44.6</a> and elementary arithmetic, we reduce to the case of a proper curve. This case follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AYV" data-tag="0AYV">33.44.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>